    // 0.28.0: the F12 menu was reorganised from 27 sections (some sharing a number) into seven,
    // with shorter key names. A user's saved values must survive that: BepInEx keeps every line of
    // the file it hasn't bound yet as an orphan (ConfigFile.OrphanedEntries, BepInEx 5.4.23,
    // checked on the installed BepInEx.dll), and Bind takes its value from the orphan with the same
    // section and key. So BEFORE anything is bound, each old (section, key) orphan is renamed to its
    // new (section, key); Bind then loads the user's value as if the file had always been written
    // that way, and the next save drops the old line. A new key that already has a value is never
    // overwritten. Three pairs of settings that only ever worked together became one setting each
    // (Merges below), computed from both old values. Nothing here runs again once the old lines are
    // gone (it only acts on orphans that exist).
